{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Let's first find the expression for $h'(x)$ and then evaluate it at $x=2$.\n\nThe derivative of $h$ can be found using **the power rule**:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^n)=n\\cdot x^{n-1}$\n\n(Remember that this applies even when $n$ is a negative number.)","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}h'(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{-5}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-5x^{-5-1}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{The power rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-5x^{-6}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"So we found that $h'(x)=-5x^{-6}$, which can also be written as $-\\dfrac{5}{x^6}$.\n\nNow let's plug $\\blueD{x=2}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n-\\dfrac{5}{(\\blueD{2})^6}\u0026=-\\dfrac{5}{64}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $h'(2)=-\\dfrac{5}{64}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $h(x)=x^{-5}$.\n\n$h'(2)=$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"answerForms":["proper","improper"],"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":-0.078125}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"h prime of 2","multipleNumberInput":false,"size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
